# Cloudflare applies these headers to every route.
# Content-Security-Policy beyond frame-ancestors is intentionally not set here — getting it
# right requires auditing every inline script (incl. Astro ClientRouter) and the Cloudflare
# Analytics beacon. Revisit a full CSP post-launch.
#
# frame-ancestors: who may iframe this site.
#   'self' is now the load-bearing one (2026-08-28). The Studio is EMBEDDED at
#   /studio on this same origin, so the Presentation tool's draft-preview iframe
#   (/preview/**) is a same-origin frame. Remove 'self' and live preview goes blank.
#   The https://*.sanity.studio / sanity.io entries are left in place only until the
#   old hosted mas-monograms.sanity.studio deploy is retired (docs/PENDING.md); the
#   localhost:3333/3334 entries served the old standalone `sanity dev` server, which
#   no longer exists — the Studio runs at localhost:4321/studio with `npm run dev`,
#   which is same-origin and therefore already covered by 'self'.
# Modern browsers prefer CSP frame-ancestors over X-Frame-Options when both are present.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://*.sanity.studio https://www.sanity.io https://*.sanity.io
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Quote-email header art (scripts/generate-favicons.mjs, referenced by absolute URL from
# src/lib/quote-email.ts). The filenames are versioned (-v1), so they can be cached for a year:
# change the art by writing -v2 and updating the URLs, never by overwriting -v1.
/brand/email-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Mary Ann's brand kit (scripts/generate-brand-kit.mjs, the Studio's "My brand kit" pane).
# Downloads are same-origin links from /studio, so no CSP grant is needed.
# Not for search engines: a ZIP or PNG cannot carry a noindex tag, so the header does it.
# Every file except the ZIP keeps Cloudflare's default (revalidate each time), because those
# names are NOT versioned. The ZIP name IS versioned (-v1), so it is cached for a year: change
# the kit by writing -v2 (KIT_ZIP in src/lib/brand/brandKit.ts), never by overwriting -v1.
# Keep Cache-Control on ONE rule per file: Cloudflare joins the values of every matching rule.
/brand-kit/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/brand-kit/mas-monograms-brand-kit-v1.zip
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
